{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791588621,"nonce":"PeLPDhshPB10mGcgBVykEYt0G30=","message":"Reactive classes (user chose this design for state in CSS): Div::class_when(name, signal) in 9ef0cc97. The class is added and removed on a live node and the stylesheet's rules for it apply and stop applying in place. Mechanism: the class's rules are layers over the node's underlying props (the same snapshot the state passes keep), so removal drops the layer and refolds the snapshot with what is left. Applied at the end of the base style passes (initial value read from the source) and by the drain on a change; the id-path state pass puts the class layers back after it resets a node; a bound write is also laid over them. Limit, documented on the method: only rules whose subject is the node itself are re-evaluated, so a descendant or sibling selector that depends on the class waits for the next full style pass.\n\nMigrated with it, each recorded from the old widget first and compared exactly (under the pinned theme), with no subtree rebuild on any interaction: cn::checkbox (cn-checkbox--checked), cn::radio (cn-radio--selected), cn::toggle_group, cn::breadcrumb links; earlier in this stretch the core toggle, checkbox, radio, button and cn::button. Tree-level tests check the stylesheet rules really move with the state (checkbox_checked_class.rs, radio_selected_class.rs, class_when.rs).\n\nOne test changed meaning: the DSL test that counted nodes to see the checkmark appear now counts shown nodes, because the mark is always present and hidden while unchecked.\n\nLeft on Stateful in cn (each needs its own look): navigation_menu, tabs (cn-tabs-trigger--active), sidebar (cn-sidebar-item--active), tree (cn-tree-node--selected), select and combobox items (--selected), resizable, number_input, input_otp, collapsible and accordion (animated structure), slider (halo), popover (user closure of is_open), pagination (a list: needs For, 746993e), dropdown_menu. The class-driven ones (tabs, sidebar, tree, select, combobox, nav links) can now use class_when.","files":null}]}